body:
Rebased to the latest.

@lyuma I have responded to the code review comments, but fundamentally, the design of the ManyBoneIK class is based on other nodes (BoneConstraint3D and SpringBoneSimulator3D) already merged, as mentioned in https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/110120#discussion_r2470526241. Therefore, I assume there is not much we can specifically address here as it should be resolved at the same time as those other nodes.

I suppose the design of the internal struct mentioned in https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/110120#discussion_r2470526241 could be improved, but since the problem is how to deal the internal array, I believe it can definitely be sent as a future follow up without breaking compatibility.

@x0r-b0t It seems to be an issue with the dynamic bone axis direction calculation by [mutable_bone_axis](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/111815). I'll take a look.

*Edited:*
I sent a fix as https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/113055.
